course: dictionary
lesson: 14855
title: Rapt: caught up in something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rapt means so interested in something that you notice nothing else around you. Look at the clues in the sentence: «The class listened with rapt attention as Miss Patel read the last chapter.» If the children were listening that closely, they were not looking at the clock or chatting to friends. So rapt means completely caught up.
explain: Rapt can also show wonder or joy. «The baby gazed, rapt, at the bubbles floating past.» The baby was not just looking. The baby was filled with wonder and could not look away. Ask yourself: what is the person paying attention to, and how do they feel about it?
explain: You will often see rapt in phrases. «Listen rapt» means you listen with all your attention. «Rapt in thought» means your mind is so busy with an idea that you miss what is happening around you. Read the words after rapt to see which meaning fits.
fact: Rapt is an adjective, so it describes a person or a feeling.
fact: «Rapt» means so caught up in something that you notice nothing else.
fact: «Rapt» can also mean filled with deep joy or wonder.
fact: «Rapt attention» means you are listening or watching with your whole mind.
fact: Synonyms for rapt include enthralled and spellbound, but rapt often shows a quieter, deeper focus.
exercise: «The class listened with rapt attention as Miss Patel read.» What does rapt mean here? | *So caught up in something that you notice nothing else | Late for school | Bored and tired of the story | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «Ravi was rapt in thought, so he did not hear his name called.» Why didn't Ravi hear? | He had his headphones in | *He was so busy thinking that he noticed nothing else | He was too far away to hear | He was fast asleep
exercise: Which word could replace rapt in «listen rapt» and keep the same meaning? | *Enthralled | Angry | Bored | Hungry
test: «The baby gazed rapt at the bubbles floating past.» What feeling does rapt show here? | Hunger for a snack | *Wonder and full attention | Tiredness after a long day | Anger at the bubbles
test: Which sentence uses rapt correctly to show full attention? | The audience sat rapt because they were rapt in sleep. | The audience sat rapt, so they all went home early. | The audience sat rapt in a loud and messy room. | *The audience sat rapt as the magician began his trick.
exam: «Ella was rapt with wonder at the night sky.» What does rapt mean? | Cold and shivering | *Filled with wonder and so caught up that she noticed nothing else | Sleepy and yawning | Lost and worried about the way home
